{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1381868-2e-territories-questions","id":1381868,"title":"[2E] Territories Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-16T00:21:59-07:00","id":1381868,"title":"[2E] Territories Questions","content":"Some questions about Territories, as understand as concept in <b>WtF</b>...<br /> <br /> 1. <b>How Territory boundaries are set?</b> When do we know when one Territory starts and second ends? In some magical way they are marked?<br /> 2. <b>Can Uratha <i>sense</i> ( in some magical way ) that they are on the Territory of other pack? </b>My players are about to cross this terrain and I wonder would they feel it?<br /> 3. <b>Do pack Territory stretch to the <i>Hisi</i>l?</b> Even with the Spirit Court in area and local Spirit Lord, that sustain fealty to pack?<br /> 4. <b>Is Protectorate treated as megaTerriotory of all involved packs?</b> Even with mystical side of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-16-2020, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T07:05:39-07:00","id":1381912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1381868-2e-territories-questions#post1381868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <b>How Territory boundaries are set?</b> When do we know when one Territory starts and second ends? In some magical way they are marked?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunting Ground rite and the Boundary Ward Gift, for magical purposes, delineated by whatever borders the pack can enforce in the long term.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. <b>Can Uratha <i>sense</i> ( in some magical way ) that they are on the Territory of other pack? </b>My players are about to cross this terrain and I wonder would they feel it? </div> </div> </div>Sight, smell, and spirits will give a lot of context clues, but there's no innate sense for crossing the threshold of a pack's claimed area.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. <b>Do pack Territory stretch to the <i>Hisi</i>l?</b> Even with the Spirit Court in area and local Spirit Lord, that sustain fealty to pack? </div> </div> </div>Hunting Ground doesn't specify anything to suggest it's limited to one of the two worlds that mostly share geography but pack territory works like gang turf. Hunting Ground will help ease relations, but Supplication and similar rites may be needed to keep a pissed-off <i>Dihir</i> from blocking you out of the area later and/or sending a message to stop you from laying claim to that chunk of space again.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. <b>Is Protectorate treated as megaTerriotory of all involved packs?</b> Even with mystical side of things? </div> </div> </div>Forge Alliance specifically doesn't apply its benefit to rites, so no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-16-2020, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T21:20:29-07:00","id":1382675,"title":"","content":"Connecting general question with my plot idea\u2026<br /> 5. <b>Hunters in Darkness are all about \u2018Sacred Territory\u2019. </b>In corebook, it\u2019s even implied they can declare Sacred Hunt on those that disturb their boundaries. ( See quote below. ) Is it possible for the Mennina pack to grant crossing right for local vampires Covenant ( Lancea Sanctum ), <b>but still be overprotective of their lands from other Uratha? Enough for the calling Siskur-Dah on clueless newcomers on their terrain that Hunts themselves there? </b>Or do they much more relate to \u2018friendly\u2019 reminder who\u2019s land it is?<br /> <br /> To give a bit more context, Hunters in Darkness pack I have in mind is much more interested in being friends with vampires than look over their Territory, so the Beshilu rats are on the rise in it. ( Cause HiD \u2018do not do their job\u2019. ) Guys like those would go after newcomer PCs that stumble on their land?<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darknes</b>s, <b>WtF</b> 2E quote:<br /> <i>\u2018The First Tongue term the Hunters use for their territory is mus-rah, or \u201choly killing ground,\u201d and that should tell you all you need to know about their views on territory. (\u2026) What constitutes a violation of mus-rah? It depends on the Hunters in question. Despoiling loci and bringing toxic resonance into the territory, certainly. Following Siskur-Dah into a Hunter\u2019s territory, perhaps. For some packs, even setting foot within their territories without formal invitation is enough. Others might let clueless humans pass through without issue, but you can be damn sure that anything entering a Hunter\u2019s territory is being watched, either by the Hunters themselves or by bound spirits.\u2019</i><br /> <br /> 6. <b>I assume that \u2018over-protective\u2019 pack of HiD simply use Boundary Ward Gift and set it on the checking Uratha in their locals, yes? </b>The same pack from my example will clearly not seek vampires by it \u2013 cause it would ping a lot if Covenant have crossing rights \u2013 and maybe not setting it on the Hosts, as they overlooking things? On the other hand, <i>Mennina </i>pack that not setting up detecting Hosts in their area is doing something wrong \u2013 so they probably set it up, in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T09:04:17-07:00","id":1478911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1381868-2e-territories-questions?p=1382675#post1382675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Connecting general question with my plot idea\u2026<br /> 5. <b>Hunters in Darkness are all about \u2018Sacred Territory\u2019. </b>In corebook, it\u2019s even implied they can declare Sacred Hunt on those that disturb their boundaries. ( See quote below. ) Is it possible for the Mennina pack to grant crossing right for local vampires Covenant ( Lancea Sanctum ), <b>but still be overprotective of their lands from other Uratha? Enough for the calling Siskur-Dah on clueless newcomers on their terrain that Hunts themselves there? </b>Or do they much more relate to \u2018friendly\u2019 reminder who\u2019s land it is?<br /> <br /> To give a bit more context, Hunters in Darkness pack I have in mind is much more interested in being friends with vampires than look over their Territory, so the Beshilu rats are on the rise in it. ( Cause HiD \u2018do not do their job\u2019. ) Guys like those would go after newcomer PCs that stumble on their land?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very late answer, but...<br /> Three birds of different species sit in the same tree, singing their songs to warn interlopers that they own that tree. They ignore each other, but go ballistic if a male of like kind comes near. Same with the Uratha: Other Uratha on the premises gets their hackles up. Vampires, being generally non-spiritual, are as irrelevant as any humans provided they don't cause trouble for the pack or stir up the spirit world. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T11:58:38-07:00","id":1479024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1381868-2e-territories-questions?p=1478911#post1478911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very late answer, but...<br /> Three birds of different species sit in the same tree, singing their songs to warn interlopers that they own that tree. They ignore each other, but go ballistic if a male of like kind comes near. Same with the Uratha: Other Uratha on the premises gets their hackles up. Vampires, being generally non-spiritual, are as irrelevant as any humans provided they don't cause trouble for the pack or stir up the spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It must be said, though, that not all birds will ignore all other species. Likewise, not all Uratha will ignore everything non-Uratha. Those things are loosely defined by design, not accident.<br /> <br /> Territorial beings will see others as a threat to their territories based on personal views. A pack of wolves may ignore humans and dogs in their territory, another pack of the same species may try to fend off dogs or move if they can't. Or they may not see dogs as a threat to their territorial claim, but fend off cows.<br /> <br /> Likewise, everything about the Uratha heavily depends on how the pack defines those things. If a pack sees vampires as concurrent predators or other kind of threat, then they are. This is also a part of the spiritual aspect of the Uratha, because at the same time that all their stuff is empowered by the fact they're also spirits, so most of their mechanics are roughly equivalent to bans, banes, Influences and so forth, on the other hand they are, at the end of the day, <i>individual spirits</i>, so they're not actually bound to have homogeneous rules about them, instead each Uratha is a unique <i>aspect</i> of the concept of Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T04:35:28-07:00","id":1479126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1381868-2e-territories-questions?p=1479024#post1479024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It must be said, though, that not all birds will ignore all other species. Likewise, not all Uratha will ignore everything non-Uratha. Those things are loosely defined by design, not accident.<br /> <br /> Territorial beings will see others as a threat to their territories based on personal views. A pack of wolves may ignore humans and dogs in their territory, another pack of the same species may try to fend off dogs or move if they can't. Or they may not see dogs as a threat to their territorial claim, but fend off cows.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a generalization. The point is, the pack has some flexibility as to who they guard against. My new players are trying to figure that out right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}